	(text "[2]AUDIO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.132 22.352 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 5.08 5.08)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "f4cd9bb6-5b3c-4702-9fb1-b67b617031c4")
	)
	(text_box "Audio Codec\n===========\n\nDecoupling capacitors\n\nFor each supply pin (or each supply \"domain\" pin):\n\n1× 100 nF MLCC placed right at that pin (same side, shortest loop to GND)\n\nPer rail (shared):\n\n1× bulk cap (typically 4.7-10 µF) near the codec on that rail\n\nThis gives:\n\nHF stability (100 nF)\n\nMF/LF charge storage (bulk)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 260.35 125.73 0)
		(size 129.54 43.815)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6f44e000-0682-4e38-a2bf-a0644eae297d")
	)
	(text_box "Audio Amplifier\n===============\n\nGain = 33K / 22K = 1.5V/V\n\n- Input capacitor C_input\n\nIn the typical application, an input capacitor, Ci, is required to allow the amplifier to \nbias the input signal to the proper dc level for optimum operation. In this\ncase, Ci and Ri form a high-pass filter\n\nC_input = 1 / 2*pi*22k*fc, for fc around 15Hz.\n\nC_input = 480nF  \n\n- Bypass capacitor C_bypass, from the datasheet\n\n1 / C_bypass * 230K < 1 / C_input * R_input\n\nC_bypass > C_input * 22 / 230 \n\n- Ouput capacitor C_output\n\n\nIn a typical single-supply, single-ended (SE) configuration, an output coupling capacitor (C(C)) is\nrequired to block the dc bias at the output of the amplifier, thus preventing dc currents in the load. As\nwith the input coupling capacitor, the output coupling capacitor and impedance of the load form a high-pass filter governed by\n\n\nf_c = 1 / 2*pi*R_load*C_output\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 260.985 174.625 0)
		(size 128.905 74.295)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c0bd7117-f389-4177-be45-dec12647acdd")
	)
